{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]I walked out tonight, for a ramble round
I didn't mean to stay, just to view the [B]town
When I saw her [A]smilin' from a [E]far
As she walked into [G][B]that crossroads [E]bar
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]Well I walked inside and sat me down
Ordered sweet red wine and I drank it [B]down
She came and [A]set beside me [E]there
With her dark brown [G]eyes [B]and the red, red [E]hair
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Solo break}
[E]I told her that I love her true
Anything you want I'll surely [B]do
Said a man like [A]you don't get too [E]far
With a girl like [G]me [B]from the crossroads [E]bar
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]I like smokey lights and a lonesome song
And I won't do right if I can do you [B]wrong
You want the moon to [A]burn behind the darkest [E]star
And you won't find [G]love [B]at the crossroads [E]bar
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Solo break}
[E]Come all my friends and take my advice
Keep your love at home with your lovely [B]wife
You're better off [A]than you think you [E]are
And you won't find [G]love [B]at the crossroad [E]bar
{end_of_verse}
